ns prologos::ocapn::crypto

;; ========================================
;; Ed25519 cryptographic operations — Phase 58.b
;; ========================================
;;
;; Foreign-function bridge into libsodium via crypto-ffi.rkt.
;; Provides the Ed25519 primitives needed to build OCapN's
;; signed op:start-session handshake.
;;
;; The FFI bindings here do NOT carry a `:requires (CryptoCap)`
;; annotation, and the header used to claim they all did.
;;
;; They should, and it is not currently possible. `:requires` on an FFI
;; binding makes the whole module UNIMPORTABLE from a `.prologos` file:
;; the requirement propagates to the caller, and there is no way to
;; introduce a root capability anywhere in the chain, so every consumer
;; fails at load with "E2001: Required capability CryptoCap not
;; available in scope. Add it as a function parameter". Wrapping the
;; bindings in same-module functions does not help — the wrapper carries
;; the requirement — and neither does importing the capability type.
;;
;; `prologos::ocapn::tcp-testing` is cited as proof the convention is
;; live. It is not: that module tags every binding `:requires (NetCap)`
;; and CANNOT BE IMPORTED either. Nothing imports it, and its test loads
;; it through the sexp `imports` path, which does not hit the same
;; check — so the breakage has no witness. Verified 2026-07-29 by
;; requiring each module from a one-line `.prologos` probe.
;;
;; So this is a LANGUAGE gap, not an OCapN one: the capability system
;; has no root introduction form, and until it does, `:requires` is
;; expressible only in modules nothing imports.
;;
;; So the annotations are absent and the `CryptoCap` import below is
;; retained as the marker for where they go. Keypair handles are opaque Nats;
;; bytes payloads (signature, pubkey, message) are carried as
;; Latin-1-encoded Strings — the same convention used by
;; `syrup-bytes` in the wire codec.
;;
;; Wire shapes built ON TOP of these primitives (gcrypt-style
;; s-expressions for pubkey + signature, signed location payload)
;; live in `captp-core.prologos`'s session-bytes builder.

require [prologos::core::capabilities :refer (CryptoCap)]

;; ----------------------------------------
;; Primitive FFI bindings
;; ----------------------------------------

;; Generate a fresh Ed25519 keypair. Returns an opaque handle to a
;; (pubkey, secret-key) pair stored in the FFI's handle table. The
;; handle stays valid until `close-keypair-raw` releases it; nothing
;; releases it automatically, and no current caller releases it at all
;; — a session key is generated once and held for the life of the
;; process. Anything that generates keypairs in a LOOP must release.
foreign racket "crypto-ffi.rkt" [crypto-gen-keypair :as gen-keypair-raw : Unit -> Nat]

;; Extract the 32-byte raw Ed25519 public key for a keypair handle.
;; Returned as a Latin-1 String (32 chars, each char = 1 byte).
foreign racket "crypto-ffi.rkt" [crypto-pubkey :as pubkey-raw : Nat -> String]

;; Sign a message (Latin-1 bytes-as-string) with the keypair's
;; private key. Returns the 64-byte detached signature as a
;; Latin-1 String.
foreign racket "crypto-ffi.rkt" [crypto-sign :as sign-raw : Nat -> String -> String]

;; Verify an Ed25519 signature. All three arguments are Latin-1
;; Strings of raw bytes: (public-key, message, signature).
foreign racket "crypto-ffi.rkt" [crypto-verify :as verify-raw : String -> String -> String -> Bool]

;; Release a keypair handle, zeroing the secret key first. Returns
;; true if the handle was present.
foreign racket "crypto-ffi.rkt" [crypto-close-keypair :as close-keypair-raw : Nat -> Bool]
